From 02593bc48a6c426d503dc164bcfdf584b868feec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 10:23:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mcp): catch the student name lists the language-center
 filter missed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The real run found 8 language-center posts with student names that were
published: six used 〇 as the mask character, two listed full names
without masking. The detector now also covers 〇 (but not in Chinese
numerals like 二〇二六), x/X masks, full and partly masked student ids,
and unmasked name lists under list-like titles.

A record that was published but is rejected on re-verification is now
set to 'withheld' and no longer served, and the daily list walk does not
reactivate it. A local reverify:<source> trigger re-checks every stored
detail in batches after rule changes. Also decode &times; and other
common HTML entities.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FCgoUnzqQSfKjvqShB2hjh
